WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.480
Rygar, you and Rygar, the legendary warrior of Argyll must defeat the evil king and his army of dangerous beasts.

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:31.080
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:32.160
I'm Mike.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:33.840
I'm Sean. And I'm Joe.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.760
And guys, today we are talking about Rygar.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:40.760
Rygar. Yeah, it's almost like it sounds like a place.

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:44.880
It does. I didn't realize that the hero was Rygar.

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:46.760
I guess the places are ghoul.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:49.260
I was thinking more like a Reptar sort of thing.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:52.660
Oh, okay. It's almost like the way the Rugrats pronounce Reptar.

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:56.940
They're like, Rygar. I haven't seen it in a long time.

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:58.720
Yeah, I was going to say, I'm not so sure about that.

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:00.240
They say Reptar or something.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:02.500
You know, Reptar was on ice, why wasn't Rygar?

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:04.120
That's true. There should have been ice levels.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:05.200
I think there was ice.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:06.340
Wasn't there ice? No ice.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:08.900
No ice? No ice. Oh, no. I meant like an actual musical.

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:09.720
Oh, like a musical.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:11.960
Like a stage performance thing that we could see.

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:13.400
But no, I don't even remember any ice in the game.

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:14.900
Maybe there wasn't. Maybe I'm thinking of something else.

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:16.180
But we're getting ahead of ourselves here.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:18.800
Hockey maybe. We need to talk about Rygar.

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:20.780
All right? We got to talk about what this game is.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:21.880
So who is Rygar?

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:23.700
Rygar is, well...

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:24.580
Or what is Rygar?

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:26.380
Yeah, are you going to get philosophical with me here?

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:27.640
Like, who is Rygar?

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:30.260
Essentially, this is like a...

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:32.380
Is Rygar a person, a concept?

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:33.420
Yeah, he's a person.

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:38.580
Okay. And this is like, I guess I would, you know, open world sounds silly here, but that is the

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:39.400
idea essentially.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:45.520
It is. It's like an open world RPG where you play as the main character, Rygar, and you kind

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:53.400
of have to trek through the world of Argyll and find the five items that the gods are demanding

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:56.560
of you. And you have this, like, spinning disc.

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:57.520
Think of it like a yo-yo.

00:01:57.540 --> 00:02:00.080
I think that's probably the best way to describe it to the viewers.

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:02.100
Because it always comes right back to you.

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:04.060
It's actually pretty short, all things considered.

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:07.300
Honestly, the weapon on the chain gave me a little bit of a God of War feel.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:13.640
Okay, yeah, yeah. So, like, think of you as Kratos, except for now you're in the mystical world of Argyll,

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:17.720
and essentially there's this evil guy, if you can believe it, called Ligar.

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:19.120
Ligar with an L.

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:24.840
Yeah. And Ligar has, like, you know, brought terror to the world, and now it's up to you to collect

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:29.420
those five items that we mentioned earlier and, you know, restore peace.

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:32.660
So, Joe, how are you going to go about doing that?

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.340
So, let me give you what I first thought this game was.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:38.260
When you first start this game, it looks like it's just a 2D side-scroller.

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:40.580
I immediately got, like, Russian attack vibes.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:41.980
Yeah? Yeah. A bit.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:46.320
Yeah. Well, obviously not the weapon, but, you know, like, just that style of game.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:49.220
Yeah. And at first I was like, yeah, this seems okay.

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:52.640
It was like, the level was a little confusing at the very first level.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:57.340
But once you find the way out of that level, you're on an open-world map.

00:02:57.640 --> 00:02:59.080
And it's completely unexpected.

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:02.700
Yeah. I had no idea the first time that I tried this.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:04.720
But then if you look in the manual, you can see the map and stuff.

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:09.580
You actually have, like, a pretty good indication of, like, okay, I have to find this place first.

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:18.060
And you go from each location on the map is its own, usually side-scrolling level, with its own enemies, its own boss and everything.

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:24.360
So it really kind of feels like a bit of an adventure to find these items you need to eventually defeat Ligar.

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:26.160
Yeah. And there's definitely exploration in there.

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:29.060
Sean, were you a fan of the exploration aspect?

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:30.560
I was a fan.

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:40.080
This game, while it's a little generic in its fantasy setting, I would say, I'd say that it does a really good job of giving you a sense of place.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:47.300
Because it really does feel like everywhere that you're going is sort of geographically a unit.

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:51.080
So between the...

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:53.880
So all the regular stages are side-scrolling.

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:58.320
And then when you open up a certain door, you end up on...

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:04.200
In, like, a top-down, almost Zelda-like plane.

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:08.480
Yeah. And even the way that you move from screen to screen is very Zelda-like.

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:11.640
Although I did notice that the screen scrolls with you for a while.

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:12.900
Yeah, yeah. Before you move to the next screen.

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:14.660
They're bigger blocks, I guess.

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:21.280
But, yeah, I like the way that it sort of all feels like it's its own little world.

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:31.360
So, you know, if I can break the walls here for a second and just ask, like, in terms of your guys' exploration of this world, how did you go about finding things?

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:35.060
Was it truly just, like, poking through everything you could do?

00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:36.340
Did you look through the manual?

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:37.740
Did you go online?

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:40.340
I used the map in the manual.

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:41.300
Okay. There's a map in the manual.

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:49.100
I used it a lot. But I will say that I liked the exploration enough that by the end of this game, it kind of felt like I didn't need the map anymore.

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:50.220
Like, I remember where things were.

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:57.520
Like, the overworld map was built in a way where it felt like you remember it.

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:01.320
Like, they felt like places I knew by the end of it, which I thought that was a really cool, you know.

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:03.080
And it's also not a huge game.

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:04.720
So there's only, you know, what, six?

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:06.740
Six different, like, main locations?

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:10.020
Well, there's, yeah. There's five dungeons, I think.

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:14.060
Okay. Yep. Sean, how did you tackle the exploration part of it?

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:22.480
I started out just by dicking around, going in different directions, seeing what kind of dead ends I'd run into.

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:33.080
And once I sort of felt like I'm getting nowhere like this, I did look into the manual and see that I was supposed to go to one place almost immediately.

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:38.200
And so I went and did that and then sort of continued to blindly move forward.

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:40.500
And I did make some progress that way.

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:48.580
But I would say that it definitely has a lot of, like, features that you can use as landmarks.

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:59.960
But I think, by and large, the, like, the hub area is a little too samey everywhere for it to be, like, perfect for me to just learn it.

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:06.020
Yeah, if you don't see that map in the manual, if you don't see that, because that does give you, like, a pretty good scope of, like, where you are.

00:06:06.140 --> 00:06:09.220
But if you don't see that, you can get lost in here pretty fast.

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:16.600
Sure. And also there's no, without seeing that map in the manual, there's no indication that, like, maybe there's an island I should go to.

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:19.680
Or maybe there are things on the edge of the coast.

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:25.200
But I'll offer that I didn't look at anything before getting to the overworld.

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:26.720
And I just kind of did the exploration.

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:39.560
And I immediately was able to find the grappling hook, which was kind of interesting that, like, it was intuitive enough that the first item you're required to get to continue on with the dungeons was the very first thing I was able to get.

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:44.220
That was like you just felt like you were supposed to go that way.

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:46.000
Okay. Which is interesting.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:54.900
My first run, so they're all sort of situated in a way, I guess, that you would find the grappling hook first.

00:06:55.120 --> 00:07:00.660
But I ended up almost getting up to the clouds before I even got the grappling hook.

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:01.640
Oh, yes.

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:03.900
Yeah. Where they tell you about the city in the sky.

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:07.260
Yeah. I went and I saw, like, you want to go there.

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:09.980
And I was like, oh, no, I don't have anything yet.

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:10.980
Yeah. Right, right. Right.

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:22.620
And it's really cool because that's another, like, thing that they've placed in the game here, you know, level design, where they're like, okay, this is a good point to tell people, like, hey, just so you know, you should have collected a grappling hook by now.

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:29.180
Right. And even though you can't do anything with it yet for that particular thing, it's just like a way to remind you of, like, hey, look for that grappling hook.

00:07:29.180 --> 00:07:32.580
And that's the other part of what informed me on where to go.

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:41.060
I would look in the manual to see where, you know, where the place with the grappling hook is because somebody in the game told me I need the grappling hook to go any further.

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:44.740
So I thought it was, granted, I did have to go back to the manual to find the map.

00:07:44.740 --> 00:07:51.060
I thought it did a good job of in-game giving you, like, your objective, like, you have to talk to people and you have to, well, those people, those bald guys.

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:52.840
Right. The same people you saw everywhere.

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:56.680
Yeah. They're, like, they're called legendaries or something like that.

00:07:56.860 --> 00:08:01.380
Yeah. In the manual, it refers to them as, like, go to meet the legendary.

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:03.920
But then some of them are called Indoras.

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:06.940
But not all of them. Yes, the Indoras give you the items.

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:08.380
Give you the items. Yeah, they're the five.

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:19.920
Yep, exactly. Basically, what we're talking about is you'll happen upon these doors, whether you're in one of the side-scrolling levels or in the overworld, like, top-down one.

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:23.380
And you'll be on, like, a pedestal.

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:25.460
No, no, you'll be on this little platform.

00:08:25.620 --> 00:08:28.720
And you'll see this giant bald, not bald.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:31.060
Yeah, he's bald. He's bald and bearded.

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:32.740
And buff. The three Bs.

00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:35.640
The three Bs of being a guy.

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:38.220
Yeah. Just sitting on this pedestal.

00:08:38.440 --> 00:08:47.800
And then you'll get a nice little box of text saying either some obscure hint or saying, like, hey, why don't you rest here for a while?

00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:53.680
Or my favorite one of them says, if you see Durago, ask him to release my daughter.

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:56.140
He just says that.

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:59.100
He's telling everyone, like, hey, if you see Durago, tell him to release my daughter.

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:00.460
There's a few like that, though.

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:02.780
There's another guy that's like, fight, fight, fight.

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:04.680
I'm like, is he just egging me on?

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:10.260
Like, you know, I didn't know what was happening because usually, to Sean's point, they're inspired, you know?

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:16.240
Like, they're trying to be, like, enlightened people who know, like, who know this great riddle that they're asking you to solve.

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:21.560
Well, but I'll offer that, like, you know, the riddles aren't necessarily, like, that complicated.

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:25.820
And most of the time, it's more just, like, poking you about doing something.

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:30.140
Like, hey, you got that crossbow, right?

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:32.240
Because otherwise, you better leave this state.

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:36.240
Yeah. Or it would be like, oh, you can get this item by going to the northwest.

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:38.280
And I was like, what are they talking about?

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:39.600
Until I found the overworld map.

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:40.820
And I was like, oh, there's a north.

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:43.620
Right, right, right. Yeah, I think it's funny, actually.

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:52.660
If you don't look at the manual and you don't know enough about this game and you just go into this game and you're on that side-scrolling level, I think we should just talk about that first.

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:54.080
Like, your experience. What is it?

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:57.000
It's like a mountain. It's called the Grand Mountain.

00:09:57.240 --> 00:09:58.980
Not Grand. Grand.

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:02.120
Like, we're going to Grand's house.

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:05.140
Yes. A thing I say every weekend.

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:12.380
Yeah. So, you're on this mountain and, you know, it's just kind of, it's like a training wheels kind of thing.

00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:14.640
Yeah. You learn a lot of things about the game this way.

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:21.740
Like, annoying things, you know, enemies will respawn whenever, wherever, however they want.

00:10:21.740 --> 00:10:24.020
But I think that that is necessary.

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:25.980
I love that the enemies respawn.

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:27.480
But we'll save that. We'll get into that.

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:28.580
Yeah, we'll get into that.

00:10:28.740 --> 00:10:40.880
But I think, like, for me, I'm going to say why that's annoying, though, because, first off, it's like, there's not, you know, there's a thought to level design in certain games where, you know, the enemies are carefully placed throughout.

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:45.500
And in this one, you know, enemies would appear right behind me.

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:47.460
They would just spawn, like, immediately behind me.

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:56.660
I'm okay with enemies spawning, like, into the area that you're currently in or spawning in, like, places that would make sense, like a regeneration spot.

00:10:56.660 --> 00:11:00.840
If we talk about, like, Kid Icarus with those pots that the worm guys would fall out of.

00:11:00.900 --> 00:11:03.520
Like, that makes sense. These worms are always going to spawn out of there.

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:08.660
These giant red scorpion things would just appear behind my back.

00:11:08.660 --> 00:11:10.300
I'd be like, how did I not see that?

00:11:10.300 --> 00:11:18.000
Yeah, they do appear close. But I do think that this game has a very quick, not that it's an excuse for it, but it has a very quick reaction time.

00:11:18.100 --> 00:11:20.880
Like, you can turn and hit almost, like, in a frame.

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:22.360
Yeah, they've got very tight controls.

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:29.740
But, like, in terms of that, like, what is our main, like, source of interacting with the world?

00:11:29.740 --> 00:11:33.040
It's just jumping and using your whirly gig, right?

00:11:34.680 --> 00:11:37.180
So, you only have that one weapon.

00:11:37.180 --> 00:11:49.500
And it's interesting because with a game, the main, like, calling card for this game, I think, is the fact that you have these power-ups that are permanent.

00:11:50.280 --> 00:11:53.160
But they're mostly all just for, like, getting around.

00:11:53.420 --> 00:11:57.220
Yeah, the items are all exploration-based, if you think about it.

00:11:57.340 --> 00:12:03.120
You have the grappling hook, which will allow you to climb up and down different areas.

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:06.760
Usually an area or something is locked behind an item, for the most part.

00:12:06.860 --> 00:12:10.420
Yeah, in some ways, that's like a Metroid element thing, you know, where it's like...

00:12:10.420 --> 00:12:11.560
Before Metroid, yeah. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:13.340
No, both these things, yeah, it's funny.

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:17.020
We're talking about Zelda and Metroid, but this game comes before both of those.

00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:20.340
And, you know, so you have the grappling hook, which will help you get out of those situations.

00:12:20.440 --> 00:12:24.280
You have the crossbow, which doesn't work anything like how I thought it would work.

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:26.420
Yeah. I actually thought the crossbow was gonna be a weapon.

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:28.260
Right. Because one of the gods mentions it.

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:30.880
And then I'm like, oh, cool, so there is another weapon in this game.

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:35.500
And then it's like, no, you'll actually just use that to create a zip line between two points.

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:44.000
Yeah, you shoot a rope. And I think that that's really a missed opportunity, because the basic gameplay loop is pretty basic.

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:51.960
I mean, I just said that, but you are really just using your armor yo-yo to hit things,

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:57.100
and you get different ways to unlock certain doors, pretty much.

00:12:57.560 --> 00:13:02.860
And I think if they're gonna have these power-ups, I would hope that there would be a new way to fight,

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:06.800
like a crossbow or some more interesting melee weapon.

00:13:06.900 --> 00:13:11.640
You know what I mean? Well, yeah, and I think that, you know, that ties into the biggest thing about this game that we haven't talked about yet,

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:15.120
which is the, you know, the progression system for your character.

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:18.420
There is, you know, a strength and defense.

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:20.480
It's called Tone and Last.

00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:27.140
Yeah. And that's a stat that upgrades throughout the entirety of the game by killing enemies, different enemies.

00:13:27.380 --> 00:13:30.120
Some enemies will give you Tone, some enemies will give you Last.

00:13:30.680 --> 00:13:37.580
And, you know, you're powering up as a person, and the only way that you really see that progression is by doing, you know,

00:13:37.720 --> 00:13:39.840
by taking less hits on an enemy.

00:13:40.020 --> 00:13:43.820
Right. Well, also, usually take four, could maybe be killed in one if you're strong enough.

00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:47.860
Yeah. Right. And as for the last, though, you can see that because you get more health.

00:13:48.300 --> 00:13:54.340
Right, right, right. And they, I didn't realize until after I played it that certain enemies give you Tone and certain enemies give you Last.

00:13:54.540 --> 00:13:58.780
Yeah. So I was thinking I was getting, when I was getting more health, I was like, I'm also getting more power.

00:13:59.080 --> 00:14:00.000
Oh, interesting. Yeah.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:00.960
But I guess that's not the case.

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:04.600
It's not the case because I'm pretty sure that would have broke the game, if you think about it.

00:14:04.660 --> 00:14:07.240
If, like, you were just constantly leveling up both.

00:14:07.560 --> 00:14:08.940
Yeah. I mean, that's...

00:14:08.940 --> 00:14:10.340
I just thought maybe it wasn't...

00:14:10.340 --> 00:14:13.060
Not to say this game isn't already a little broken.

00:14:13.260 --> 00:14:15.020
It's a little, I think it's got some jank to it.

00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:17.800
All right. Yeah. There are things, certain things.

00:14:17.900 --> 00:14:22.220
I think the biggest thing for me is that you can despawn enemies by walking away.

00:14:22.360 --> 00:14:24.620
Yes, exactly. Yeah. But I don't think that was enough.

00:14:25.560 --> 00:14:31.900
The enemies are so frequent that it's, to me, like, the levels were still relatively challenging,

00:14:31.900 --> 00:14:33.620
even with the ability to despawn the enemies.

00:14:33.620 --> 00:14:38.580
Okay, but the despawn of the enemies, though, that comes from, like, that is a memory glitch.

00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:39.860
Like, that is, like...

00:14:39.860 --> 00:14:44.100
Yeah. You know, I don't know how they would have avoided that since they wanted them to be, like,

00:14:44.460 --> 00:14:48.720
you know, planned encounters in a game that's filled with random encounters for those enemies

00:14:48.720 --> 00:14:50.420
that you can specifically, like, despawn.

00:14:50.540 --> 00:14:55.600
But essentially, it's like, you're getting close enough to the edge where they're no longer seen.

00:14:55.600 --> 00:15:00.760
Yeah. That, like, if you went back any further than that, they would come back into that same place.

00:15:00.760 --> 00:15:07.260
But if you just manage to clip them off the edge, the way that the memory works on the NES is kind of like the very first,

00:15:07.260 --> 00:15:16.660
if we imagine them as, like, vertical frames, the very first vertical frame and the last vertical frame on your TV are kind of like the same memory.

00:15:16.660 --> 00:15:21.460
So it's knowing that, like, hey, there's nothing on this side, so there shouldn't be anything on that side.

00:15:21.640 --> 00:15:23.000
Yeah, it's like the game...

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:24.620
And that's a very basic explanation.

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:27.500
Like, that's not the truth, but that's the way that'll help us explain this.

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:32.460
I think a more layman's way is this game just lacks object permanence.

00:15:32.860 --> 00:15:35.660
Like, as soon as it exits the screen, it no longer exists.

00:15:35.800 --> 00:15:42.860
Right. And even weirder about that, though, is that, like, that's what makes the random encounters necessary in the game

00:15:42.860 --> 00:15:49.140
because you have to grind, you know, to get through these, you know, to level up and power up

00:15:49.140 --> 00:15:51.360
and be able to be strong enough to defeat the bosses.

00:15:52.560 --> 00:15:58.300
But the way that the random encounter in this game is handled is it becomes a little bit of a mess.

00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:00.320
Yeah. And it's easily exploited.

00:16:00.700 --> 00:16:02.060
Yeah. Very easily exploited.

00:16:02.160 --> 00:16:03.240
Yeah, it's easy to grind. But I don't know.

00:16:03.320 --> 00:16:06.220
It didn't bother me too much the way that they spawned close to you.

00:16:06.420 --> 00:16:12.200
I felt like when they were spawning close to me, I kind of felt like it gave you the opportunity to feel kind of badass.

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:13.960
You're like, because you have to move so fast.

00:16:14.100 --> 00:16:15.760
And, yeah, I mean, you got hit sometimes, too.

00:16:15.840 --> 00:16:18.920
I'm not even talking about the problem with, like, I'm getting hit very often.

00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:28.600
And that is a problem because, you know, HP in this game isn't something that you necessarily have access to at any given time.

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:31.100
You mean, like, health power-ups or anything like that?

00:16:31.100 --> 00:16:33.320
Yeah, or even just, yeah, like the ability to recover your health.

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:36.320
Yeah, recover. It's only done through spells, which we'll cover in a minute.

00:16:36.320 --> 00:16:42.120
But other than that, you have to hope for a drop of a potion, which is only going to restore one health point.

00:16:42.380 --> 00:16:46.800
Yeah. So if you think about how long it takes you to get one of those, how many random encounters you'll experience,

00:16:46.800 --> 00:16:53.120
and how many enemies might get in the way to the point where you just don't have a way to get through all of them,

00:16:53.120 --> 00:16:56.820
you'll take the hit and be worse off because of it.

00:16:56.840 --> 00:16:58.840
I feel like I had a different experience.

00:16:59.100 --> 00:17:00.060
Okay. Let's hear it.

00:17:00.060 --> 00:17:02.980
Yeah. I also think I did a lot more fighting.

00:17:03.100 --> 00:17:09.300
And we were talking about this just before we started recording, that I must have grinded a lot more at the beginning

00:17:09.300 --> 00:17:13.680
because it was taking me fewer hits to kill some things that I was watching you fight that was taking you more hits.

00:17:13.840 --> 00:17:17.280
Right. So I was probably already, like, a little more leveled up.

00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:19.460
So that might have made it easier.

00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:27.120
But I felt like the health potions were dropped enough to at least keep me consistent at a health level.

00:17:28.040 --> 00:17:34.300
Like, if suddenly I'm like, oh, I'm low at health, I would just stand in one spot where I knew some, like, basic, like, some nothing crazy,

00:17:34.580 --> 00:17:39.460
like, some basic enemies would show up, and I'd be able to hit them enough to get a few health potions back.

00:17:39.680 --> 00:17:45.800
Okay. But also when you – I know we didn't cover this yet, but when you hit them enough, you get these other points.

00:17:45.900 --> 00:17:46.800
What are they called again?

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:49.400
The point that you spend.

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:51.380
I call them stars points.

00:17:51.560 --> 00:17:54.000
But, yeah, I think their stones is probably the right way to go.

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:58.200
So there's these stars that allow you to spend points on three different things.

00:17:58.680 --> 00:17:59.880
One of them is –

00:17:59.880 --> 00:18:00.740
Well, they're your spells.

00:18:01.100 --> 00:18:04.560
Right. Those are spells that you specifically cast as Rhaegar.

00:18:04.620 --> 00:18:07.100
And one of your spells is regain all of your health.

00:18:07.320 --> 00:18:13.740
And I used to – I used to – I would save all of my star points up for the health thing.

00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:18.180
So I would always in my back pocket have, like, restore all my health to kind of get me out of a sticky situation.

00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:20.300
So what are the other spells?

00:18:21.540 --> 00:18:28.580
There's power-up, which is really weird because you cast it once, and it's good for the entire game.

00:18:28.760 --> 00:18:30.740
Oh. The entire game.

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:35.080
Unless you die. But, like, it's something that you would get back pretty quickly.

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:37.440
Yeah, yeah. It costs the least amount of points.

00:18:37.740 --> 00:18:41.100
I think it's – I think it uses three points.

00:18:41.100 --> 00:18:42.880
And they're called mind points.

00:18:42.880 --> 00:18:45.040
That's what it is. It's the – you know, like –

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:46.740
Mind. It says mind, and then you have, like, a meter.

00:18:46.740 --> 00:18:51.700
It only costs three points to cast this power-up spell, and then you're immediately stronger.

00:18:52.000 --> 00:18:54.600
Your yo-yo thing goes out faster.

00:18:54.600 --> 00:18:55.760
I don't think it makes you stronger.

00:18:55.800 --> 00:18:58.160
I thought it just made your thing – your weapon longer.

00:18:58.160 --> 00:19:01.540
It says here that – oh, yeah, yeah.

00:19:01.540 --> 00:19:03.260
Allows the grappling – this is in the manual.

00:19:03.480 --> 00:19:05.840
Allows the grappling hook weapon to be stretched.

00:19:06.440 --> 00:19:07.480
So, yeah. Right. Okay.

00:19:07.520 --> 00:19:11.620
It's a grappling hook? It says grappling hook, but –

00:19:11.620 --> 00:19:14.900
Interesting. Yeah, that's why when I first read that, I was like, oh, I don't need that.

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:16.800
I thought it was talking about the grappling hook.

00:19:17.060 --> 00:19:18.440
Right, which can extend to infinity.

00:19:18.860 --> 00:19:21.680
Yeah. You have the world's longest grappling hook.

00:19:22.960 --> 00:19:28.180
But – and then you have attack and assail, which I actually thought at first – I was like, oh, this is kind of silly.

00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:35.000
But man, does it pay off in those boss fights because it's almost like a lightning strike for, like, ten attacks.

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:42.460
But it's only your very first ten attacks, so you can't use it and then say, like, oh, I'm going to save this for later because you have to use it right away.

00:19:42.620 --> 00:19:45.620
But it attacks everything on the screen.

00:19:45.860 --> 00:19:47.900
Every time you use your thing.

00:19:48.060 --> 00:19:55.540
Every time, yeah. Every time you use a thing, regardless of if your weapon makes contact or not, it just destroys the things on the screen.

00:19:55.540 --> 00:20:01.680
Wow. I think it's also useful if you're in a spot with particularly hard enemies that keep spawning.

00:20:01.860 --> 00:20:03.660
Right, exactly. And you need to get out of a jam.

00:20:03.660 --> 00:20:15.680
You need to get moving. But still, I was – I felt like – I felt more comfortable saving all those points for recover because then I could always get myself out of a jam.

00:20:15.700 --> 00:20:17.100
I think, yeah, I think recover is money too.

00:20:17.120 --> 00:20:24.720
It's a good strategy. Yeah. Recover is good because you would save that until you're at your very end of your life because it's always going to restore all of your points.

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:31.880
You know, something that isn't necessary when you only have four health points, but by the end of the game when you have 12, I could see some use in that.

00:20:31.880 --> 00:20:32.740
Got some value to it. Yeah.

00:20:32.800 --> 00:20:34.560
Right. All right.

00:20:35.120 --> 00:20:38.020
So, Joe, this is a section I know you've been dying to talk about.

00:20:38.260 --> 00:20:42.940
In the manual, they refer to the enemies as –

00:20:42.940 --> 00:20:48.160
They refer to them as – instead of monsters or enemies –

00:20:48.160 --> 00:20:49.180
Bestiary. Yeah.

00:20:49.320 --> 00:20:53.640
They say this is our list of animalized men wriggling eerily.

00:20:54.300 --> 00:20:55.440
So poetic.

00:20:55.800 --> 00:20:57.260
It's beautiful in a way.

00:20:57.260 --> 00:21:01.120
We're fighting. We're fighting animalized men wriggling eerily.

00:21:01.280 --> 00:21:03.940
I didn't think there was any eerie wriggling going on.

00:21:04.140 --> 00:21:05.460
It really is a beautiful sentence.

00:21:06.060 --> 00:21:12.280
Yeah. And I guess I could – I didn't really think about it, but maybe these guys are like humans who have been transformed into those animals.

00:21:12.400 --> 00:21:14.580
I mean, Ligar has created like hell on earth.

00:21:14.760 --> 00:21:16.400
And to be honest, this place doesn't look that bad.

00:21:16.400 --> 00:21:22.160
I mean, I'm watching some footage right now, and I definitely just saw like a scary tree.

00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:23.980
But like I don't think that was a dude.

00:21:24.100 --> 00:21:24.960
I think that was just a tree.

00:21:25.100 --> 00:21:28.820
But don't you think this is the world that Rigar has like just always lived in?

00:21:28.960 --> 00:21:32.320
Like it doesn't look like there was ever a civilization here, period.

00:21:32.320 --> 00:21:38.220
That is something I wanted to – okay, so I'm sorry to get away from the monsters, but that is something that I wanted to address.

00:21:38.460 --> 00:21:43.700
Like this is apparently like a kingdom or a place that used to have some civilization.

00:21:43.740 --> 00:21:48.200
And aside from the gates, like there's no buildings.

00:21:48.200 --> 00:21:50.500
There's nothing – there's no infrastructure.

00:21:51.160 --> 00:21:55.940
Except for some zip lines and some gates, there's no proof of human existence on this island.

00:21:55.940 --> 00:21:57.200
Rigar did that. Rigar did all that.

00:21:57.280 --> 00:21:58.240
Rigar did all of this.

00:21:58.240 --> 00:22:02.000
I'd have to – I just want to know like even what's Rigar's like backstory?

00:22:02.200 --> 00:22:03.420
Like why is he the guy?

00:22:03.600 --> 00:22:08.920
I think he was dead. Yeah, he was resurrected to fight Rigar because you need a rhyming person to fight a bad guy.

00:22:09.440 --> 00:22:12.280
It's one of those – the five legendaries rules.

00:22:12.500 --> 00:22:14.220
Yeah, it needs the rhyme.

00:22:14.540 --> 00:22:17.360
Yeah, that's the game story for you.

00:22:17.960 --> 00:22:23.140
Once there was a holy place called Argyll, which was founded by five legendary Indora gods,

00:22:23.180 --> 00:22:26.160
and then suddenly the blackest tragedy happened.

00:22:26.160 --> 00:22:31.020
That's – you know, it's the most dramatic manual I've read to date.

00:22:31.860 --> 00:22:40.460
But yeah, I guess my experience with this manual is strange because like I checked it out after you told me about animalized men wriggling ear.

00:22:40.460 --> 00:22:41.640
I was like, I have to check this out.

00:22:41.880 --> 00:22:44.800
Then I found a bunch of cool tips that I would have never found out.

00:22:44.900 --> 00:22:52.100
And then I realized like if you don't have the internet, if it's 1987, like you can't buy a used copy of this game.

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:54.640
You need the manual to do anything.

00:22:54.640 --> 00:23:00.880
Don't lose the manual. Well, you could have bought the NES – isn't there like a –

00:23:01.280 --> 00:23:02.740
The Nintendo Player's Guide.

00:23:02.880 --> 00:23:04.860
Yes. Or you could have called that hotline.

00:23:05.320 --> 00:23:06.420
Nintendo have a hotline.

00:23:06.700 --> 00:23:09.380
Yeah, Nintendo did have – the Nintendo Power had a hotline.

00:23:09.460 --> 00:23:11.060
And even Toys R Us had a hotline actually.

00:23:11.060 --> 00:23:12.740
You could call them just Toys R Us.

00:23:13.000 --> 00:23:16.480
And I guess they had someone who was just a resident expert of playing games.

00:23:17.400 --> 00:23:19.740
There's another thing though with manuals since we're on that topic.

00:23:19.740 --> 00:23:21.820
I don't know if it's going to happen in any NES games.

00:23:22.080 --> 00:23:27.100
But one thing that they used to do is like a form of DRM would be like in your manual.

00:23:27.480 --> 00:23:33.780
Oh, yeah. You know, it would have like a specific code for you like on those old DOS games.

00:23:34.080 --> 00:23:36.280
You know, and it would be like you have to type this into the computer.

00:23:36.440 --> 00:23:38.940
And that was like their serial key, if you will.

00:23:38.940 --> 00:23:45.620
But also to prove that you didn't like give it to your friend, you know, and you'd have to do everything if you wanted to do it that way.

00:23:45.800 --> 00:23:49.420
I guess like it's not the exact same thing and I don't want to get too off topic.

00:23:49.600 --> 00:24:00.920
But the example for that that I always think back to is for Metal Gear Solid 1, you have – the character, I think it's Otacon, tells you – no, no, no.

00:24:00.920 --> 00:24:09.720
It's the kernel, tells you to look at the back of the CD to get like the frequency for somebody you're supposed to call on your radio.

00:24:10.280 --> 00:24:13.320
And it only exists on the back of your box.

00:24:13.680 --> 00:24:17.860
So thank goodness we have game FAQs like today to help us out there.

00:24:17.980 --> 00:24:21.680
But honestly, like things like that, interesting, right?

00:24:21.680 --> 00:24:26.780
Because it is like a cool way to involve you directly into the story.

00:24:26.840 --> 00:24:32.100
But at the same time, you're like, you know, I don't want to take my CD out right now and look at that thing.

00:24:32.220 --> 00:24:33.080
Like I don't need that.

00:24:33.320 --> 00:24:38.700
And it's like sooner or later all CDs and all physical media will just be gone anyway.

00:24:38.940 --> 00:24:42.440
Not because of an impending apocalypse that we keep talking about every episode.

00:24:42.440 --> 00:24:43.400
No, it might happen though.

00:24:43.560 --> 00:24:44.700
No, I know. But also just like –

00:24:44.700 --> 00:24:46.100
Don't lie to our audience like that.

00:24:46.440 --> 00:24:47.840
CDs are in retrograde.

00:24:48.780 --> 00:24:49.740
Just like Mercury.

00:24:49.920 --> 00:24:50.900
Everything's going to hell.

00:24:52.180 --> 00:24:53.200
Let's get back to the game.

00:24:53.200 --> 00:25:00.040
What are we talking about? But if there is an apocalypse, we have a vault full of cassette tapes for the next few episodes of Nostalgia that you can uncover.

00:25:01.320 --> 00:25:02.580
Absolutely. I think that's a good time for it.

00:25:02.580 --> 00:25:06.880
If some legendary warrior wants to uncover the Nostalgia backlog.

00:25:08.060 --> 00:25:09.100
Anyway, what's up, Mike?

00:25:09.260 --> 00:25:10.820
I was going to say it's a good time for a break.

00:25:11.320 --> 00:25:39.500
Okay. And you know, it's funny.

00:25:39.660 --> 00:25:42.680
We were talking earlier about the progression system.

00:25:42.680 --> 00:25:48.060
And I, you know, again, because I'm not checking this manual religiously, I didn't know about this actually.

00:25:48.060 --> 00:25:53.260
I wasn't like – I wasn't aware that I was getting stronger because it doesn't necessarily feel like it.

00:25:53.300 --> 00:25:59.100
Yeah. And so I didn't know about this progression thing until I got to the first boss in the game.

00:25:59.520 --> 00:26:03.140
And I remember texting you, Joe, and being like, what do I do?

00:26:03.260 --> 00:26:04.220
Like, what's the secret?

00:26:04.320 --> 00:26:07.460
Because I knew you were into the game and you probably got him further than that.

00:26:07.580 --> 00:26:09.120
And I was like, I just don't get it.

00:26:09.320 --> 00:26:13.120
Because I was doing like 100 hits to the boss.

00:26:13.120 --> 00:26:16.820
Yeah, the first boss is the one that just shoots up the three fireballs.

00:26:17.140 --> 00:26:17.980
The three fireballs. Yeah.

00:26:18.500 --> 00:26:21.540
It's ridiculous. Like, if you don't grind –

00:26:21.540 --> 00:26:22.740
And you have to grind a lot.

00:26:22.880 --> 00:26:26.920
Because I – even after that, I was like, oh, okay, grinding's the secret apparently.

00:26:27.080 --> 00:26:28.220
Didn't know there was progression in this game.

00:26:28.300 --> 00:26:29.200
But sure, let's go with it.

00:26:29.780 --> 00:26:37.900
Grinding's the secret. I must have grinded for like 20 minutes and it still wasn't enough to do like – you know, it still took like 60 shots to knock him out.

00:26:38.000 --> 00:26:41.600
See, this was also before I realized that grinding was doing anything.

00:26:41.600 --> 00:26:43.480
But other than giving me health.

00:26:43.600 --> 00:26:44.700
And I knew my health was increasing.

00:26:44.980 --> 00:26:51.200
So I was – you know, I guess I was grinding on that first level just while I was playing but not realizing that's what I was doing.

00:26:51.640 --> 00:26:58.300
But when I got to it, I was having a lot of trouble with it because there's not a lot of space to weave between those three fireballs that's shooting at you.

00:26:59.240 --> 00:27:05.180
But eventually my strategy was just I got enough points to have a recover available.

00:27:05.180 --> 00:27:11.820
And I just would jump in there, take as many hits as I could while hitting them as many times as I possibly could.

00:27:12.200 --> 00:27:14.620
Once my health was low, recover, do it again.

00:27:14.800 --> 00:27:16.960
And not even on the second time, it just killed them.

00:27:17.080 --> 00:27:18.400
Joe, we're playing two different games.

00:27:20.060 --> 00:27:20.960
I did that.

00:27:21.860 --> 00:27:26.460
And I even had our audio producer, Chris, watch me do it again today.

00:27:26.980 --> 00:27:29.100
And it still just wasn't enough.

00:27:29.620 --> 00:27:31.760
It wasn't enough for the – what's his name?

00:27:31.920 --> 00:27:33.060
Aruga the first one?

00:27:33.160 --> 00:27:35.100
It just wasn't enough for Aruga.

00:27:35.220 --> 00:27:36.840
Aruga. E-R-U-G-A.

00:27:36.840 --> 00:27:38.380
I got words for Aruga, okay?

00:27:38.540 --> 00:27:43.580
Who is also just like another generic two-headed dog thing.

00:27:43.780 --> 00:27:44.820
Like that's a thing.

00:27:44.980 --> 00:27:46.300
I thought he was more of like a turtle.

00:27:46.480 --> 00:27:47.480
Is he not a – All right, turtle.

00:27:47.500 --> 00:27:51.420
Sure, whatever. But like I see multiple heads on an animal and I'm like, that's a dog.

00:27:51.420 --> 00:27:58.420
Well, about the enemy design and bosses, like I think the enemy design in general is pretty good.

00:27:58.580 --> 00:28:01.620
Like there's some cool variety in what you're going to be fighting.

00:28:01.800 --> 00:28:05.760
But the bosses are really underwhelming.

00:28:05.980 --> 00:28:07.220
That's what I thought too.

00:28:07.420 --> 00:28:09.800
Yeah. I thought they were relatively easy.

00:28:10.040 --> 00:28:12.460
I mean, yeah, they're not complicated.

00:28:12.880 --> 00:28:16.980
And aside from just the fact that if you're too weak, you have to brute force them.

00:28:17.080 --> 00:28:18.940
They're not scary.

00:28:18.940 --> 00:28:23.480
Yeah, the only thing they've really done to the bosses is just add a ton of HP to them.

00:28:23.540 --> 00:28:28.540
Yeah. Because if you think about it, some of the – like who are those robots that show up?

00:28:28.660 --> 00:28:30.940
Oh, yeah. The robots – I think it's just Mr.

00:28:31.060 --> 00:28:32.780
Robot. We're my second least favorite.

00:28:33.120 --> 00:28:35.260
Those robots that just show up though, first off, that's random.

00:28:35.380 --> 00:28:38.180
And another like, you know, I'm curious about the lore here.

00:28:38.460 --> 00:28:41.780
Like, you know, they're not going to give me anything, but I'd love to know.

00:28:41.780 --> 00:28:43.000
I've never seen any technology in this game.

00:28:43.360 --> 00:28:47.140
Ligar actually comes from the future to go through the past and then –

00:28:47.140 --> 00:28:50.880
Well, I had assumed though – because I called those robots in my notes too, but I assumed

00:28:50.880 --> 00:28:53.800
that I was just seeing them as robots and they were meant to be something else.

00:28:53.860 --> 00:28:58.700
Are they robots? If you look in the manual, in the Wiggling Beasts and Where to Find Them –

00:28:58.700 --> 00:29:00.740
Wiggling Beasts and Where to Find Them.

00:29:00.820 --> 00:29:02.960
They are called – there's something robotic.

00:29:03.000 --> 00:29:04.580
Super Robot Bargain.

00:29:04.680 --> 00:29:05.640
Oh, it's a bargain.

00:29:05.920 --> 00:29:09.880
No, no, no. But it's like B-A-R-G-A-N.

00:29:09.920 --> 00:29:10.920
So it's like Bargan.

00:29:11.200 --> 00:29:12.100
Like, or Bargon.

00:29:12.600 --> 00:29:15.800
But no, it's not an O, so it can't be Bargon, but Bargan.

00:29:16.520 --> 00:29:22.640
Bargan. Yeah, and it was designed for the purpose of having command of the sky of Lapis and is

00:29:22.640 --> 00:29:26.160
capable of discharging deadly electromagnetic superwaves.

00:29:26.480 --> 00:29:27.540
I definitely felt those.

00:29:27.660 --> 00:29:30.200
I think he's harder than some of the bosses, I guess is what I'm getting at.

00:29:30.380 --> 00:29:31.260
And also more interesting.

00:29:31.760 --> 00:29:33.560
It's like, oh, here's this crazy robot.

00:29:33.740 --> 00:29:36.560
Different mechanic. And then you go to the boss and it's like, oh, it's a spider.

00:29:37.860 --> 00:29:42.840
Well, I also thought another enemy that was at least more annoying than the bosses are

00:29:42.840 --> 00:29:47.640
those weird three-piece dragon things that, like, they fly around.

00:29:47.640 --> 00:29:49.080
Okay, well, they're not three-pieces, Joe.

00:29:49.660 --> 00:29:51.180
Are they wearing a three-piece suit?

00:29:51.200 --> 00:29:53.500
No, look at them. There's three, like – they're almost like a caterpillar.

00:29:53.600 --> 00:29:55.720
They have, like, three sections of their body in, like, a staircase.

00:29:55.720 --> 00:29:58.360
You mean the shoulders, the stomach, and the butt?

00:29:59.360 --> 00:30:00.260
That's what I'm seeing.

00:30:00.420 --> 00:30:01.260
I'm seeing, like –

00:30:01.260 --> 00:30:03.400
All right. Listeners, look up a picture of them.

00:30:03.420 --> 00:30:06.720
You'll see what I mean. And the shoulders, the stomach, and the butt are very separated.

00:30:07.080 --> 00:30:08.960
All you've done to explain them are three-piece dragon.

00:30:09.140 --> 00:30:10.800
They can't look up three-piece dragon.

00:30:11.080 --> 00:30:13.040
These guys are – You can look up the manual.

00:30:13.300 --> 00:30:16.580
They're called, like, Ep-O-Con.

00:30:16.820 --> 00:30:18.220
Ep-E-P-O-Con.

00:30:18.520 --> 00:30:19.440
Yeah. You know what? Yeah.

00:30:19.480 --> 00:30:23.060
You have to say it just like that because you, too, will be confused about how to pronounce

00:30:23.060 --> 00:30:25.940
things that have O and I right next to each other.

00:30:26.100 --> 00:30:27.520
Oi. Ep-O-A-Con?

00:30:30.580 --> 00:30:31.880
Oh, okay. Thank you, listener. Ep-O-A-Con.

00:30:31.880 --> 00:30:36.060
I don't know. It's a flying dragon which has been living in a primeval mountain.

00:30:36.380 --> 00:30:40.420
He will attack Rygar by dropping eggs of a snow-gruce.

00:30:41.140 --> 00:30:43.940
Didn't know there were snow-gruce eggs. Didn't know that there was a living creature in those eggs.

00:30:44.040 --> 00:30:45.720
Yeah, snow-gruces are off-camera.

00:30:46.180 --> 00:30:50.280
Those things – They're very big compared to, like, a lot of the enemies, and they – it doesn't

00:30:50.280 --> 00:30:53.180
seem to stop them from spawning, like, several of them on the screen.

00:30:53.360 --> 00:30:54.880
Yeah. It just takes up, like, half the screen.

00:30:55.060 --> 00:30:59.060
That's one of my random encounter arguments, Joe, is that, like, you see, like, three of those

00:30:59.060 --> 00:31:01.160
guys spawned on the screen at different heights, too.

00:31:01.240 --> 00:31:04.840
So you've got, like, the guy really low, and then the guy really high, so it's like, well,

00:31:04.900 --> 00:31:06.220
I can't jump or anything.

00:31:06.420 --> 00:31:10.540
And then the guy who's really low gets to a point where, like, even if you duck, he's

00:31:10.540 --> 00:31:12.080
just going to drop that egg right on your head.

00:31:12.160 --> 00:31:13.280
Right. Like, good luck.

00:31:13.420 --> 00:31:15.240
My strategy with M2 is take it slow.

00:31:15.260 --> 00:31:17.100
As soon as I see one, kill it immediately.

00:31:17.340 --> 00:31:19.700
Don't go further and allow more to spawn.

00:31:20.620 --> 00:31:23.820
This game – this whole game is take it slow to the game because you might as well just

00:31:23.820 --> 00:31:26.380
continue to let creatures respawn to kill them anyway.

00:31:26.380 --> 00:31:30.500
So there's no reason to rush through a stage because ultimately that's just going to leave

00:31:30.500 --> 00:31:32.140
you really frustrated with a boss.

00:31:32.420 --> 00:31:40.160
Yeah. I feel like you guys are very negative on the grinding, which I get.

00:31:40.480 --> 00:31:43.340
But to me, it was – I don't know.

00:31:43.480 --> 00:31:46.060
It was just – it was satisfying to kill a bunch of enemies.

00:31:46.420 --> 00:31:47.880
Like, I didn't notice it as much.

00:31:47.900 --> 00:31:49.820
Well, here's another thing about the grinding.

00:31:49.820 --> 00:31:56.340
And maybe there have been some games released on the PC during this time that it had that

00:31:56.340 --> 00:32:01.180
as a concept. But I – is this the first grinding game that – I mean, it's definitely the first grinding

00:32:01.180 --> 00:32:02.620
game that we've played. I think it is.

00:32:02.620 --> 00:32:05.920
Yeah. It's the first grinding game that we've played on the NES.

00:32:05.920 --> 00:32:11.380
Yeah. And I think what's interesting is, like, I'm not saying that the grinding itself is

00:32:11.380 --> 00:32:13.800
bad. Right. I'm not saying that the progression is bad.

00:32:13.800 --> 00:32:20.120
It's a mix of my argument that the random encounters aren't handled properly and Sean's

00:32:20.120 --> 00:32:25.580
argument that, like, the basic line of combat isn't enough to keep your attention.

00:32:25.920 --> 00:32:31.560
You know? Grinding in Final Fantasy is interesting because you continue to, like, think about new ways

00:32:31.560 --> 00:32:32.760
to use your squad.

00:32:33.000 --> 00:32:38.020
Like, you know, am I going to attack these guys with magic or, you know, my raw power?

00:32:38.020 --> 00:32:40.720
Or am I going to use this sword instead of that wand?

00:32:40.900 --> 00:32:43.620
Like, you know, there's things to think about there.

00:32:43.800 --> 00:32:47.000
Whereas here, it's really just like, all right, I'm going to wait for the dragon to

00:32:47.000 --> 00:32:47.900
come to my level.

00:32:47.900 --> 00:32:49.400
And then I'm going to hit him twice.

00:32:49.600 --> 00:32:51.600
And then sooner or later, I'll be able to hit him once.

00:32:51.780 --> 00:32:56.780
One thing I do want to clarify for the listener that may not have played this game, because

00:32:56.780 --> 00:33:04.340
random encounter is more of an RPG, like, turn-based battle sort of word.

00:33:04.600 --> 00:33:11.700
But he just means that instead of enemies that are clearly placed by the level designer,

00:33:11.700 --> 00:33:18.000
they just, it's almost sort of kung fu style, where they just sort of show up off screen

00:33:18.000 --> 00:33:20.640
and it doesn't matter if you killed them, there will be more.

00:33:20.980 --> 00:33:22.260
Or in the middle of your screen.

00:33:22.420 --> 00:33:23.420
Or in the middle of your screen, yeah.

00:33:23.420 --> 00:33:27.560
It's almost like if the Goombas from Zumaire Brothers, because that's like, you know, that's

00:33:27.560 --> 00:33:29.200
the similar side-scrolling title.

00:33:29.440 --> 00:33:32.900
Or like, let's just say, like, Red Devils from Ghosts and Goblins.

00:33:32.900 --> 00:33:38.520
If they just showed up wherever, you know, instead of in those carefully placed spots.

00:33:38.800 --> 00:33:41.900
Yeah. I mean, they definitely come at a specific spot.

00:33:42.020 --> 00:33:43.280
They always come at the same spot.

00:33:43.640 --> 00:33:44.740
But it's not...

00:33:45.220 --> 00:33:47.000
It's not handcrafted.

00:33:47.060 --> 00:33:47.880
It's not fixed.

00:33:48.060 --> 00:33:52.120
Yeah. But it will always be like, when you come to this screen, you'll find two of these red

00:33:52.120 --> 00:33:53.900
devil-looking things and one of these things.

00:33:54.060 --> 00:33:55.740
And then, like, they'll keep coming.

00:33:55.920 --> 00:33:58.100
Yes. But I also...

00:33:58.100 --> 00:34:00.660
I guess now that I think about it, I noticed some variation in that, actually.

00:34:00.720 --> 00:34:02.400
In the first level, everything keeps coming.

00:34:02.520 --> 00:34:06.380
But in some levels, you kill something, and then it's gone until you leave the screen.

00:34:06.760 --> 00:34:10.580
Or you can kind of wiggle around in the screen to force things, too.

00:34:10.780 --> 00:34:12.740
Like, you'll have to actually move the screen.

00:34:12.940 --> 00:34:16.020
Like, you'll have to move enough in the level for the screen to shake a little bit.

00:34:16.120 --> 00:34:19.360
Right. But if the screen starts shaking, new enemies will spawn.

00:34:19.780 --> 00:34:23.320
Right. I guess I'm just thinking of some of, like, the vertical areas where the screen doesn't move.

00:34:23.580 --> 00:34:25.660
You know, that's, for me, that's combat.

00:34:25.660 --> 00:34:29.000
But how did we feel about controls in the game?

00:34:29.300 --> 00:34:31.700
So, I think that...

00:34:32.420 --> 00:34:35.180
I think they're pretty tight in the side-scrolling levels.

00:34:36.240 --> 00:34:43.800
But when it comes to the top-down view, I just find it very strange that they...

00:34:43.800 --> 00:34:45.760
Like, you can only move in four directions.

00:34:45.760 --> 00:34:48.480
You can go left, right, up, and down if you're just walking around.

00:34:48.640 --> 00:34:52.540
You have to jump if you want to do any sort of, like, diagonal movement.

00:34:52.540 --> 00:35:01.400
And I don't understand, like, if they allow you to move diagonally while you're jumping, why can't you do that while you're walking?

00:35:01.400 --> 00:35:02.460
Yeah, I never thought of that, actually.

00:35:02.460 --> 00:35:03.360
It's a very...

00:35:03.360 --> 00:35:04.500
It just feels sticky.

00:35:04.820 --> 00:35:08.060
Like, every time you land, you're just in, like, mud or something.

00:35:08.480 --> 00:35:13.180
It's probably because they didn't, you know, like, they didn't have the animation required to...

00:35:13.180 --> 00:35:14.140
Well, they don't have to.

00:35:14.380 --> 00:35:16.020
If you jump and you go diagonally...

00:35:16.020 --> 00:35:16.860
No, and it looks silly.

00:35:16.900 --> 00:35:20.700
You look like you're just jumping forward but moving diagonally.

00:35:21.140 --> 00:35:25.740
How would you look like you were walking forward but still moving diagonally?

00:35:25.860 --> 00:35:26.860
Is that how you would look? You know, though, I think...

00:35:26.860 --> 00:35:32.740
I mean, I think even as late as Chrono Trigger, I think if you move diagonally in Chrono Trigger, you don't turn diagonally.

00:35:32.860 --> 00:35:33.760
You're still facing...

00:35:33.760 --> 00:35:34.900
I think it would work fine.

00:35:35.280 --> 00:35:36.580
I don't think it would break my immersion.

00:35:37.540 --> 00:35:38.760
I just found it very annoying.

00:35:38.900 --> 00:35:44.260
Well, yeah, exactly. With the limited things that are going on in this game anyway, I don't think it's going to break my immersion if he starts moving that way.

00:35:44.380 --> 00:35:45.280
That didn't bother me, though.

00:35:45.820 --> 00:35:48.860
I didn't mind hopping around because it's a good way to dodge everything.

00:35:48.920 --> 00:36:00.480
No, it is. You can be in the middle of jumping around and projectiles can come at you, enemies can come at you, and as long as you're in the air, they can't affect you.

00:36:00.520 --> 00:36:04.900
But if you throw your weapon, it will attack them.

00:36:05.440 --> 00:36:08.280
Yeah, and that was one of my bigger complaints.

00:36:08.540 --> 00:36:17.940
I did exploit it a little bit, but the game doesn't understand its own depth when you're on an overworld map, a top-down view.

00:36:17.940 --> 00:36:25.800
You can jump, and for the perspective, yeah, you're going higher up on the screen, but the game assumes that you're there.

00:36:25.800 --> 00:36:29.040
Yeah, you're still... I don't know if I'm explaining that properly.

00:36:29.040 --> 00:36:30.420
You're still on the same XY axis thing.

00:36:30.420 --> 00:36:35.120
I'm jumping up, and I'm hitting an enemy that's behind me because the game thinks I'm back there because I jumped.

00:36:35.340 --> 00:36:41.420
Reminds me of when we were talking about 1942 and how every plane is on the same exact part of the C axis.

00:36:41.420 --> 00:36:42.280
Until you looped a loop.

00:36:42.740 --> 00:36:46.640
Yeah, yeah. Okay, so I felt pretty good about the controls.

00:36:46.840 --> 00:36:54.160
I mean, I'll agree with you there, Joe, that it is a tight attack, and I didn't feel like it wasn't responsive.

00:36:54.160 --> 00:36:57.700
Like, oh, it just didn't get out quick enough, or oh, I couldn't turn fast enough.

00:36:57.700 --> 00:37:00.480
Like, I think those things are appropriately animated.

00:37:00.800 --> 00:37:09.320
And I think that it has some good game feel when, because it does incorporate a stun and a little bit of knockback on your enemy,

00:37:09.500 --> 00:37:12.600
like, it does feel punchy when you do hit them.

00:37:12.740 --> 00:37:16.020
You do feel like it wasn't just, oh, it registered a hit.

00:37:16.120 --> 00:37:18.440
It was actually like, oh, I definitely got this guy.

00:37:18.440 --> 00:37:26.600
And I'll also applaud them for, like, the unique way that they handled, like, all those additional items without having to, like, go to a menu and select them.

00:37:26.740 --> 00:37:31.340
It's just, like, you know, find the part where it's needed, and then, you know, like.

00:37:31.700 --> 00:37:32.840
Contextual. Yeah, contextual.

00:37:33.100 --> 00:37:39.140
Like, hit the up arrow and your attack button, and because you're near this spot, now it'll form a zip line.

00:37:39.320 --> 00:37:47.040
Or hit down and your attack button, and if there is ground below you, it will know to use the grappling hook to go lower.

00:37:47.520 --> 00:37:48.420
Thought that was cool.

00:37:48.680 --> 00:37:57.780
Mm-hmm. The items in general, though, I, you know, I'm echoing the statement from earlier, but I do wish that they would have been able to be used in a combat situation as well.

00:37:58.540 --> 00:38:06.280
Exactly. Because even the grappling hook, you know, like, think about how cool that would be if all of a sudden you're able to, like, grapple enemies, bring them towards you, and then hit them with the whip.

00:38:06.960 --> 00:38:08.020
That or. The whip.

00:38:08.520 --> 00:38:10.720
Yeah, the whip from Pennsylvania.

00:38:11.120 --> 00:38:22.660
The yo-yo. Um, because of the way that the grappling hook works in the game, there's no reason why it couldn't have been registered as a weapon if you hit somebody above you.

00:38:22.700 --> 00:38:25.480
Because it does, like, look like a projectile that you're shooting.

00:38:25.660 --> 00:38:27.840
Yeah, it won't even grab those mind stones.

00:38:28.120 --> 00:38:29.940
Yeah. Uh, or potions or anything.

00:38:30.140 --> 00:38:36.100
It won't grab anything that isn't, um, you know, like, like, other than a piece of land.

00:38:36.320 --> 00:38:37.260
Yeah. Missed opportunities.

00:38:37.520 --> 00:38:42.600
Yeah. And so now that, since we're talking about items and the exploration again anyway, let's talk about backtracking.

00:38:42.980 --> 00:38:44.920
Uh, because it's weird.

00:38:45.300 --> 00:38:47.500
At first this was, like, a problem for me.

00:38:47.640 --> 00:38:50.280
Then I was like, well, it's not really that big of a deal.

00:38:50.480 --> 00:38:52.040
Like, how else would you handle it?

00:38:52.080 --> 00:38:53.220
The levels aren't huge.

00:38:53.600 --> 00:39:04.960
So when you have to, because first you do have to backtrack a little bit on the overall map, but you also have to go back into full levels that you've been to now that you have the grappling hook or now that you have, you know, whatever, the crossbow.

00:39:04.960 --> 00:39:12.700
And I think I'm a bigger fan of backtracking in the levels because that's, like, a cool, like, neat way to go back to those levels that you've already been in.

00:39:12.740 --> 00:39:19.780
Like, imagine if you had to go back to World 1-2 and Super Mario Brothers because you just got this new thing and you gotta do it there, you know?

00:39:19.960 --> 00:39:28.500
That's cool. I don't think backtracking in the overall was necessary, and I almost kind of wish, like, after you beat the boss, you just started back at, like, you know, outside the Grand Mountain.

00:39:28.820 --> 00:39:33.700
I don't know. I sort of like the, it establishes a sense of place.

00:39:33.900 --> 00:39:40.520
Yeah. I mean, backtracking is sort of like a new concept right now, and I don't know.

00:39:40.580 --> 00:39:46.160
I think that it's needed to give you the visual memory of where you are and where you've been.

00:39:46.380 --> 00:39:56.660
And also, if you're going to backtrack to those levels, then the feeling of going back on the map to get physically to where that level is kind of puts the cherry on it, you know?

00:39:56.700 --> 00:39:58.460
It makes it feel complete.

00:39:58.620 --> 00:39:59.860
Yeah. Like, really backtracking fully.

00:39:59.860 --> 00:40:00.820
You've got that anticipation.

00:40:01.300 --> 00:40:12.820
But, yeah, it was also just cool to me that, I mean, I guess that is like a Metroid thing, but you unlock an item and you go back and you're like, oh, wait, wasn't there a, you know, there was a post here that I could shoot a grappling hook or whatever.

00:40:12.820 --> 00:40:23.260
Yeah, and you can imagine if you're into the game enough, you could have your notebook and be taking notes on like, oh, cool, this guy told me I need the crossbow for here, so I'll make a note of that.

00:40:23.320 --> 00:40:28.200
Right. And then this way I can check it later and be like, oh, yeah, now I got the crossbow, let me go back and see what was there.

00:40:28.860 --> 00:40:42.220
You know, I think the game could have even went further with this idea and even just like cool like secret areas or, you know, like new ways to get to different parts of the overworld.

00:40:42.380 --> 00:40:47.620
Right. Like, you know, imagine if there was like a cave that connected the east and west sides.

00:40:48.020 --> 00:40:50.100
Oh, yeah, yeah, like passageways and things like that.

00:40:50.200 --> 00:40:52.640
Yeah, but you could only access it after a certain point in the game.

00:40:52.780 --> 00:41:00.160
That would have been neat. Now that you're saying that too, I think that that is one thing that, granted, it's the first game to do stuff like this that I know of or that we've played.

00:41:00.260 --> 00:41:03.500
That we've played. It's definitely been done at this point, I want to stress that.

00:41:03.500 --> 00:41:06.140
And like Legend of Zelda has come out in Japan.

00:41:06.780 --> 00:41:11.520
But like, but like, you know, for the North American player, this is the first time you're experiencing something.

00:41:11.600 --> 00:41:18.100
But yeah, I do think it could have benefited from more of that stuff on the world map to more than just your destinations on the map.

00:41:18.300 --> 00:41:26.800
Yeah. I mean, right now, this whole gathering items that give you access to things that you couldn't before, they're acting as just keys.

00:41:27.040 --> 00:41:30.200
Like they may as well have just said, here's the blue key.

00:41:30.340 --> 00:41:31.400
You can use it on blue doors.

00:41:31.400 --> 00:41:36.340
Sure. But it is more fun to see like, oh, I'm creating a grappling line with this one.

00:41:36.340 --> 00:41:38.640
In the context of the game, it feels better.

00:41:38.860 --> 00:41:44.840
But I think that if they're going to introduce a new feature, it better have more than one use.

00:41:45.360 --> 00:41:47.780
Like that's just inefficient game design to me.

00:41:48.080 --> 00:41:50.680
Yeah, but most of them have, I mean, most, yeah, you do the same thing with it.

00:41:50.740 --> 00:41:54.980
But most of them have several times, like the grappling hook, you use that several different places.

00:41:55.200 --> 00:41:57.220
The grappling hook, I think, is the best example.

00:41:57.220 --> 00:42:01.520
I think the worst example is just like the crossbow.

00:42:01.720 --> 00:42:08.620
Like you will see just these lone yellow blocks that, like, oh, I guess I'm using the grappling hook.

00:42:08.680 --> 00:42:09.900
I thought they were like wooden stump.

00:42:09.960 --> 00:42:10.980
Whatever, wooden stump.

00:42:11.180 --> 00:42:12.300
I know. Yeah.

00:42:12.660 --> 00:42:20.340
But it's not like, oh, I can use my crossbow to trigger this other thing that has a completely different context in the game.

00:42:20.860 --> 00:42:22.300
Yeah, I get it. I understand what you're saying.

00:42:22.300 --> 00:42:29.620
I totally agree. I do like that they have implementation both in the overworld and in the levels themselves for the most part.

00:42:29.680 --> 00:42:36.380
Yeah. But, like, it doesn't change the fact that, like, you know, even though these are missed opportunities, I get it, Joe.

00:42:36.500 --> 00:42:37.960
You're saying this. Well, this is the first time, right?

00:42:38.120 --> 00:42:39.280
There's still problems, right?

00:42:39.400 --> 00:42:41.740
Yeah. Can you agree on that? But, yeah, there are definitely problems.

00:42:41.800 --> 00:42:44.800
No, no, I'm saying that that's still a problem even if it's the first time.

00:42:45.400 --> 00:42:51.460
I'm surprised that you said crossbow was the worst because I thought that was also very – it was cool to, like, be in a level and be like, what is this wooden stump?

00:42:51.580 --> 00:42:55.600
And then later on be like, oh, where was that wooden – like, I go back and do – like, I still see that in game design today.

00:42:55.840 --> 00:43:03.240
Like, just, like, there's things that you don't know what it is and then later on you realize, oh, this unlocks these and you go back to those levels to find those things.

00:43:03.340 --> 00:43:08.760
I like that one. I mean, like, between the – what do you call it when there's already a zipline?

00:43:09.500 --> 00:43:10.760
The item that you get so you can use it.

00:43:10.760 --> 00:43:12.080
Oh, yeah. I actually don't know what that's called.

00:43:12.080 --> 00:43:16.000
Whatever that is and the crossbow are almost, like, redundant.

00:43:16.360 --> 00:43:21.380
Like, you could have just had that be one item that you created your own for the whole thing.

00:43:21.720 --> 00:43:25.400
Sure. I mean, it just – it felt like they were – like, they were –

00:43:25.400 --> 00:43:26.980
They're stretching it. Yeah, I see that.

00:43:26.980 --> 00:43:31.080
It is weird that, like, one acts as a zipline and the other one's like, now create your own lines.

00:43:31.080 --> 00:43:34.880
And it's like, but only in these specific spots that look exactly like the zipline one.

00:43:42.980 --> 00:44:17.060
Thank you. All right, so that was backtracking somehow.

00:44:17.360 --> 00:44:19.200
We didn't even know how to give an items thing.

00:44:19.420 --> 00:44:21.360
Let's talk level variety.

00:44:21.800 --> 00:44:28.800
Yeah. Yeah, I thought there was a decent amount of variety between the levels for the most part.

00:44:29.240 --> 00:44:32.320
You would get different enemies and stuff like that.

00:44:32.380 --> 00:44:36.520
But then there was one point where suddenly one of the levels is an overhead.

00:44:37.260 --> 00:44:38.540
It's like the overworld map.

00:44:38.540 --> 00:44:39.740
You're in a dungeon.

00:44:41.260 --> 00:44:43.780
I think it's cool that they had that level variety.

00:44:44.040 --> 00:44:50.740
I don't know if the two overworld levels were executed as well as the side-scrolling levels.

00:44:50.860 --> 00:44:52.000
But I just thought it was interesting.

00:44:52.160 --> 00:44:54.080
It was kind of nice to break it up.

00:44:54.360 --> 00:44:58.820
But there was a lot of, especially in the first level, which was...

00:44:58.820 --> 00:45:01.480
The game works better as a side-scrolling game.

00:45:01.480 --> 00:45:02.740
It does. Yeah, absolutely.

00:45:03.020 --> 00:45:04.720
I think it was Durago is the name of the place.

00:45:04.860 --> 00:45:06.080
Oh, the island...

00:45:06.080 --> 00:45:07.480
Yes. That you have to get to.

00:45:07.700 --> 00:45:08.840
Yeah, so the northwest there.

00:45:09.720 --> 00:45:11.100
There was a lot of...

00:45:12.120 --> 00:45:18.440
You're on this cobblestone floor, and there's just a lot of repeating empty...

00:45:18.440 --> 00:45:19.800
There's nothing in the space.

00:45:19.880 --> 00:45:21.500
Every screen is just more floor.

00:45:21.820 --> 00:45:24.900
Yeah. And that felt a little scarce.

00:45:24.900 --> 00:45:30.120
They were trying to make it vast, but they didn't have quite enough in there.

00:45:30.120 --> 00:45:33.320
Mm-hmm. But it was cool to change it up.

00:45:33.400 --> 00:45:36.020
But that was another boss battle that was also overhead.

00:45:36.240 --> 00:45:39.700
You could kind of exploit the whole depth perception thing to beat the boss.

00:45:39.840 --> 00:45:42.240
You kind of stay below it. You jump up, hit it a bunch of times.

00:45:42.380 --> 00:45:48.080
Right. I would even disagree, though, that there's a good enough level variety in the side-scrolling

00:45:48.080 --> 00:45:56.560
stages. They were all fun enough for me, but there was some moments of deja vu with just different

00:45:57.420 --> 00:45:58.540
background assets.

00:45:58.740 --> 00:46:01.280
It's like, well, the structure of the stage is still very much the same.

00:46:01.520 --> 00:46:03.040
Go left to right.

00:46:03.440 --> 00:46:08.580
Just head right and get to your thing and dodge or attack enemies as you choose.

00:46:08.580 --> 00:46:11.500
Right. The level that stood out for me was the cave level.

00:46:11.800 --> 00:46:17.060
Yeah, same. I think that the cave level is really cool because it's actually got some dungeon design

00:46:17.060 --> 00:46:20.040
to it where you have to choose your paths, check out with the-

00:46:20.040 --> 00:46:21.520
It's got more verticality to it.

00:46:21.580 --> 00:46:22.980
Right, right. See what the legendaries have to say.

00:46:22.980 --> 00:46:25.980
There was another level that you use primarily, the grapple hook.

00:46:26.840 --> 00:46:28.120
Yeah, in the forest.

00:46:28.940 --> 00:46:30.500
Yeah, I think there was another one.

00:46:30.500 --> 00:46:33.260
Well, I mean, you use them in all the stages, but I'm talking about in the forest.

00:46:33.260 --> 00:46:35.940
There's one where you're climbing a mountain, basically, with the grapple hook.

00:46:36.040 --> 00:46:38.480
Right, right, right. To go to the Sky City.

00:46:38.580 --> 00:46:41.820
Yeah. I thought that was cool.

00:46:41.980 --> 00:46:45.960
And you're right, they don't get too different from each other.

00:46:46.160 --> 00:46:51.380
But I think another reason why it didn't bother me too much is the game is relatively short.

00:46:51.620 --> 00:46:54.200
It never, for me, felt like, oh, this is getting old.

00:46:54.380 --> 00:46:55.540
It's only five levels.

00:46:55.800 --> 00:47:00.320
Well, I mean, it's short when you have the resources that we have.

00:47:00.380 --> 00:47:05.220
But I think it's much longer for people that only have the manual to go off of.

00:47:05.340 --> 00:47:06.520
That's all I went off of.

00:47:06.520 --> 00:47:08.620
I think everything you need is in the manual.

00:47:08.740 --> 00:47:11.760
It tells you exactly where to get the things, and there's a map of where.

00:47:11.940 --> 00:47:13.780
It tells you where each item is and the map.

00:47:13.780 --> 00:47:16.600
I never struggled with what to do next.

00:47:16.800 --> 00:47:23.820
Yeah. And what's interesting is this might go as one of those games that I've booted up the most in nostalgia.

00:47:24.040 --> 00:47:27.380
I've just continued to be like, okay, I finished that.

00:47:27.560 --> 00:47:28.740
I'm going to take a break now.

00:47:28.940 --> 00:47:31.180
And then, oh, but I got to go back in now.

00:47:32.260 --> 00:47:33.440
Or I'm stuck on a boss.

00:47:33.580 --> 00:47:35.480
And then, okay, but I just want to try that thing one more time.

00:47:35.780 --> 00:47:38.600
Something about this game kept intriguing me to go back to it.

00:47:38.740 --> 00:47:41.940
Like, I didn't know what the payoff was going to be.

00:47:42.360 --> 00:47:44.220
And to be honest, the ending's not that great.

00:47:44.520 --> 00:47:46.560
But I didn't know what was going to happen.

00:47:46.600 --> 00:47:49.120
But I was just intrigued by this whole world.

00:47:49.340 --> 00:47:54.360
Yeah. And it's like a weird thing that I was able to play it in five-minute doses.

00:47:54.460 --> 00:47:56.600
But this isn't one of those games that you should be doing that in.

00:47:56.740 --> 00:47:57.700
No. I agree with Joe.

00:47:57.900 --> 00:48:00.520
It's short. It is a short game, all things considered.

00:48:00.920 --> 00:48:03.720
It's also a relatively easy game, all things considered.

00:48:03.860 --> 00:48:06.580
I wouldn't say this is an NES hard style game.

00:48:06.660 --> 00:48:08.020
I think most people could play this.

00:48:08.160 --> 00:48:11.500
The core gameplay mechanic is pretty easy.

00:48:11.740 --> 00:48:14.820
None of the enemies pose that much challenge.

00:48:15.100 --> 00:48:22.380
But I just think that this game is really hard to do in one or two sittings.

00:48:22.540 --> 00:48:25.120
And the fact that you cannot save in this game.

00:48:25.120 --> 00:48:27.340
And there's no password feature in this game.

00:48:28.440 --> 00:48:34.920
Like, kids in the 80s, I mean, there are ways to save now between, like, if you've got, like, a Retron.

00:48:34.920 --> 00:48:38.620
Or if you've got all that, like, if you're emulating or all these things.

00:48:38.760 --> 00:48:40.060
Like, you can save your progress.

00:48:40.220 --> 00:48:45.260
But you need to keep the system on if you want to make any kind of progress in this game.

00:48:45.360 --> 00:48:53.380
Right. And I just think that that is a huge oversight for, I know that you guys are saying that this is short and easy.

00:48:53.580 --> 00:48:58.100
But it still takes some time for, like, a new player, I think, to get accustomed to it.

00:48:58.100 --> 00:49:00.520
Right. And I think, but I also think that's part of the journey.

00:49:01.340 --> 00:49:02.520
You know, like, this is weird.

00:49:02.520 --> 00:49:06.060
But, like, I didn't mind replaying the beginning a few times.

00:49:06.280 --> 00:49:07.460
Like, and I did. I did.

00:49:07.740 --> 00:49:12.020
Like, when I got far enough, I was like, okay, I'm far enough now that I just want to see this thing through.

00:49:12.280 --> 00:49:17.660
But I've played, like, up to getting the grappling hook, like, a lot.

00:49:18.260 --> 00:49:31.060
Like, there's just something about, like, the fun of, like, starting in the mountain, exploring the mountain, getting to the overworld, and then acquiring the grappling hook and being like, oh, there's such a neat thing about, like, and I think it's just, like, me neat.

00:49:31.060 --> 00:49:34.560
I don't think it's, like, an actual, like, great game.

00:49:34.560 --> 00:49:40.060
I just think, like, you know, like, it's so cool for me to be seeing this as someone who's playing them in chronological order.

00:49:40.240 --> 00:49:42.920
It's just like, huh, this mechanic is everywhere now.

00:49:42.920 --> 00:49:45.240
But this is where the trend is going.

00:49:45.240 --> 00:49:47.280
And it's, like, the first one that we've seen.

00:49:47.280 --> 00:49:55.500
Yeah. I just also think, though, Sean, like, I'm not saying it's so short that you could beat it, like, in 15 minutes.

00:49:55.700 --> 00:49:59.000
But it should not take anyone who wants.

00:49:59.000 --> 00:50:00.080
You can beat it in a couple hours. Yeah.

00:50:00.200 --> 00:50:09.260
I was going to say, anybody who wants to beat the game should be, even with, like, dying and starting back up again, because you only go to the very same screen that you win.

00:50:09.340 --> 00:50:10.300
That's including boss fights.

00:50:10.380 --> 00:50:13.320
Like, if you die at the boss fight, you just go right back into the boss room.

00:50:13.320 --> 00:50:14.460
That was nice. Yeah.

00:50:14.460 --> 00:50:16.340
Because some of the bosses, yeah, it took a few tries.

00:50:16.340 --> 00:50:19.580
And if I had to play the whole level again, you would have probably backed out.

00:50:19.700 --> 00:50:20.940
Yeah. But it's a long enough game.

00:50:20.940 --> 00:50:23.160
They understand that there's not a save feature to it.

00:50:23.700 --> 00:50:28.380
And we're talking maybe, like, at most four hours.

00:50:28.720 --> 00:50:29.800
Like, tops.

00:50:29.960 --> 00:50:30.880
That's what I would say, too.

00:50:30.880 --> 00:50:37.720
If you really know this game, like, after a while, I think you can get all the way up to the ending in, like, 45 minutes.

00:50:38.060 --> 00:50:40.060
I mean, I did watch this B-run that happened.

00:50:40.140 --> 00:50:42.080
It was, like, less than half an hour.

00:50:42.180 --> 00:50:43.640
But, I mean, I get it.

00:50:43.760 --> 00:50:44.600
I get what you're saying.

00:50:44.900 --> 00:50:48.300
Yeah. Did either of you get to the final boss?

00:50:48.440 --> 00:50:49.940
No. Yeah.

00:50:50.120 --> 00:50:52.120
The Ligar. Ligar, yes.

00:50:52.380 --> 00:50:53.740
Is it the Ligar or is it Ligar?

00:50:54.180 --> 00:50:55.360
It's Ligar. His name is Ligar?

00:50:55.640 --> 00:50:57.100
Ligar. And he's green.

00:50:57.260 --> 00:50:59.500
And he has, like, two. What are those things coming out of him?

00:50:59.720 --> 00:51:01.260
They're, like, I got it written down here.

00:51:01.260 --> 00:51:02.500
You know, mouth things.

00:51:02.820 --> 00:51:05.120
I think they're, like, snakes. I thought it was, like, a lion with snake heads.

00:51:05.220 --> 00:51:06.380
Yes. I thought that's what it was, too.

00:51:06.380 --> 00:51:08.640
Is that what a chimera is?

00:51:08.680 --> 00:51:10.280
I don't know. No, but also, like, just to be clear.

00:51:10.280 --> 00:51:12.060
It's an animalized man wriggling ear right.

00:51:12.060 --> 00:51:13.300
Yes, exactly. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:51:13.400 --> 00:51:15.440
I was going to say, to be clear, he's an animalized man.

00:51:15.560 --> 00:51:19.480
But also, the snakes aren't, like, as predominant as the Ligar himself.

00:51:19.600 --> 00:51:20.680
They're just, like, these.

00:51:21.440 --> 00:51:22.840
Is he a lion tiger?

00:51:22.980 --> 00:51:24.080
Yeah, that's what I was thinking, too.

00:51:24.120 --> 00:51:25.960
Well, that's actually what I immediately went to.

00:51:26.000 --> 00:51:29.140
And then I was like, oh, yeah, but that wasn't a thing in 1987.

00:51:29.440 --> 00:51:35.680
Was it not? It's just weird that, no, the first Ligar was created, like, when, you know, like, 2000-something.

00:51:35.940 --> 00:51:37.900
Are we talking about, like, Napoleon Dynamite right now?

00:51:37.900 --> 00:51:39.640
Yeah, okay. Well, it's in the play, though.

00:51:40.200 --> 00:51:41.040
There was a real.

00:51:41.160 --> 00:51:42.160
I thought they made a Ligar.

00:51:43.280 --> 00:51:44.820
In real life, I could have sworn.

00:51:44.960 --> 00:51:46.260
Hey, maybe. I could have sworn.

00:51:46.260 --> 00:51:48.080
It doesn't sound unbelievable to me, yeah.

00:51:48.220 --> 00:51:49.440
See, thank you. They are real.

00:51:49.660 --> 00:51:52.200
Thank you, Chris. See, that's why we have our audio producer.

00:51:52.360 --> 00:51:54.820
Yes, for that reason. Just for the, because he's a Ligar expert.

00:51:55.060 --> 00:51:58.760
I forgot that he works at the zoo and is our Ligar expert.

00:51:59.360 --> 00:52:02.660
So, Sean, do you want to take back laughing at me now to my face?

00:52:02.660 --> 00:52:03.640
No, I still think it's funny.

00:52:04.000 --> 00:52:07.880
Okay. Anyway, can I, can I.

00:52:07.880 --> 00:52:08.880
Talk to me about the final box.

00:52:08.880 --> 00:52:10.640
Talk about the final level in general.

00:52:10.820 --> 00:52:15.900
Okay, yeah, yeah, yeah. Because, first of all, you climb up to this final level, which is, like, this castle in the sky.

00:52:16.100 --> 00:52:20.520
Something that is teased at the, even at the very beginning of the game, like, when you first get to that stage,

00:52:20.900 --> 00:52:25.560
enough of the legendaries will kind of, like, poke you to be like, hey, check out what's up there.

00:52:25.680 --> 00:52:31.760
And then when you finally get up there, they're like, oh, but you need these five things before you should even think about going up there.

00:52:32.040 --> 00:52:33.380
They got a nice view from the roof.

00:52:34.240 --> 00:52:37.140
But when you get up there, too, it is, I liked it.

00:52:37.220 --> 00:52:38.880
Now, looking back on it, maybe it's kind of a flaw.

00:52:38.880 --> 00:52:43.300
But you're kind of just, like, in this huge castle wall.

00:52:43.480 --> 00:52:46.860
It's, like, seven or eight screens long, and there's no door on that side.

00:52:46.880 --> 00:52:50.000
You get to the corner, and you've got to go up seven or eight more screens.

00:52:50.200 --> 00:52:51.640
But I kind of thought it was cool at the time.

00:52:51.640 --> 00:52:53.480
I was like, oh, my God, this is so vast.

00:52:53.820 --> 00:53:00.240
Right. If only, I guess, like, my response to that is, if only it was as vast as they made it seem.

00:53:00.240 --> 00:53:09.480
Like, really cool if you want to do something like that, but then to have it actually not be that, like, crazy long of a level that, like, is intricate was, like, strange.

00:53:09.480 --> 00:53:15.540
Yeah, you go through, and it's, like, it's just a bunch of very similar-looking square rooms with a bunch of shadows.

00:53:15.540 --> 00:53:16.520
The monsters are all just shadows.

00:53:16.520 --> 00:53:19.860
Yeah, yeah, they're all shadow monsters, which isn't explained in the manual as far as I know.

00:53:20.040 --> 00:53:21.000
But, like, sure.

00:53:21.260 --> 00:53:23.240
But you know. In the clouds, everybody is shadow.

00:53:23.360 --> 00:53:26.480
Right. Yes. But they do, after a while, kind of, they take their toll on you.

00:53:26.480 --> 00:53:35.060
So when I got to the boss, I only had, you know, my three health, and when you die, you always respond with your three health, even if you have room for more health.

00:53:35.260 --> 00:53:42.580
So I left and went, got my health back up, got enough points to have a recover stored away.

00:53:42.980 --> 00:53:49.540
And at a certain point, once you get the coat of arms, there are certain of the bald men.

00:53:49.540 --> 00:53:50.580
Yeah, the legendaries.

00:53:50.580 --> 00:53:57.500
There are certain guys that will just give you a life potion that's different than those little red potions that drop in the enemies.

00:53:57.520 --> 00:54:00.840
Right, this life potion you can use whenever you want, and it gives you all of your health back.

00:54:01.060 --> 00:54:05.580
But also, when you talk to those guys, they give you the potion and give you all of your health back.

00:54:06.000 --> 00:54:11.880
So I stocked up on that potion, on that recover, went back in, tried to keep my health as long as I can.

00:54:11.880 --> 00:54:13.240
And you can have two of those potions.

00:54:13.600 --> 00:54:14.960
You cannot. You can.

00:54:14.960 --> 00:54:17.120
The other space does not let you take a potion I tried.

00:54:17.300 --> 00:54:21.680
Oh, interesting. It only lets you take, what is the last item you need?

00:54:23.300 --> 00:54:24.660
The ocarina. No.

00:54:25.500 --> 00:54:26.860
Really? Yeah. The ocarina.

00:54:27.220 --> 00:54:29.400
It only lets you take a flute or something.

00:54:29.600 --> 00:54:33.900
It's what you need to do to, like, open the door to the shadow realm.

00:54:34.000 --> 00:54:36.800
Okay. Because I thought you could get two of those, but you can't.

00:54:37.180 --> 00:54:38.680
But you can exploit it completely.

00:54:38.680 --> 00:54:45.080
You can go in there as many times as you want as long as you have room for a potion, get your health fully healed, and get a potion.

00:54:45.420 --> 00:54:51.440
But I went back up to the main level, tried not to fight that much because I didn't want to lose any health, got back to the boss, and was like, okay, this is it.

00:54:52.220 --> 00:54:58.820
I'm going to just go in and attack, lose all my health, recover, attack, lose all my health, recover, attack.

00:54:59.140 --> 00:55:05.080
But I only had to attack and lose all my health once, and then on the second time, he died.

00:55:05.420 --> 00:55:06.940
So, like, it wasn't that hard.

00:55:06.940 --> 00:55:09.120
So that's just, like, that's the story of this game.

00:55:09.180 --> 00:55:11.280
I just kept hitting him, and then he just died.

00:55:11.460 --> 00:55:14.320
The level, to me, was harder than the boss.

00:55:14.520 --> 00:55:20.720
The theme of the game is hit everything in life, and you'll just get what you want.

00:55:21.060 --> 00:55:21.880
Yeah. Wow.

00:55:22.220 --> 00:55:25.240
Yeah, and then, Joe, how did you feel about the ending?

00:55:26.460 --> 00:55:30.940
It's just like a, I don't know what I'm expecting, really, I guess.

00:55:30.940 --> 00:55:38.640
But, like, from some games, you know, like smaller-sized games, when you get an ending, it's just like, congratulations, you did it at the end, right?

00:55:38.740 --> 00:55:43.700
And it's like, I guess, like, for Rygar, I was expecting, like, a more conclusive thing.

00:55:43.920 --> 00:55:48.080
But they really just kind of send you off with, like, a story of, like, peace is now returned.

00:55:48.360 --> 00:55:51.960
You've done it. Well, also, you get that really nice picture.

00:55:51.960 --> 00:55:53.020
It's just one screen, right?

00:55:53.020 --> 00:55:54.700
Of the dove. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:55:54.780 --> 00:55:56.260
The dove, yeah. Who is the dove?

00:55:56.420 --> 00:55:58.680
It's just a dove. I thought maybe that was Rygar now.

00:55:58.880 --> 00:56:00.940
Okay, you opened, okay, but you know what you did?

00:56:00.940 --> 00:56:02.420
You opened the peace door.

00:56:03.860 --> 00:56:08.020
The peace door was removed when Rygar came into office.

00:56:08.640 --> 00:56:11.100
Into office. This is a political office.

00:56:11.120 --> 00:56:20.180
When you create the peace door again, that is like, you know, it's all about the, what you guys just don't understand is this game is talking in metaphor.

00:56:20.580 --> 00:56:23.960
And the peace door stands for peace in the world.

00:56:24.740 --> 00:56:25.620
I think I got that.

00:56:25.700 --> 00:56:28.580
That's beautiful. I think I did understand that.

00:56:28.960 --> 00:56:30.240
Okay, you know what? I take it back.

00:56:30.460 --> 00:56:32.880
The ending's great. The ending's a masterpiece.

00:56:33.200 --> 00:56:35.120
And I really wish that they would just make a Rygar film.

00:56:35.280 --> 00:56:40.800
To be honest, this might say something about the ending, but when you asked me that, I couldn't quite remember how it ended.

00:56:41.020 --> 00:56:41.900
You don't remember the dove?

00:56:42.080 --> 00:56:43.600
I don't remember the dove even now.

00:56:43.860 --> 00:56:48.480
But I do remember that it's just one, like, it's like a title screen, and it doesn't go away.

00:56:48.480 --> 00:56:52.140
It's a screen that says, you know, whatever, peace has returned, yada, yada.

00:56:52.140 --> 00:56:54.880
But then I'm sitting there waiting, I'm pressing A, I'm pressing start.

00:56:55.120 --> 00:56:56.620
